crown: Pass the microphones through Amazon's ASR and Voice pipelines

The audio HAL ran Amazon's front end on every recording: its own echo
canceller, beamformer and level normalization, tuned for Amazon's wake word
engine. It fought the echo canceller the Kiosk Satellite Edition preloads
into the HAL. With the ASR and Voice pipelines in passthrough, Android gets
microphone 0 as that canceller leaves it.

diff --git a/proprietary/vendor/etc/audio-algorithms/asp.cfg b/proprietary/vendor/etc/audio-algorithms/asp.cfg
index 896bd06..b9d774d 100644
--- a/proprietary/vendor/etc/audio-algorithms/asp.cfg
+++ b/proprietary/vendor/etc/audio-algorithms/asp.cfg
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@
         },
 
         "ASR": {
-            "Passthrough": false,
+            "Passthrough": true,
             "Frame length" : 128,
             "Input": {
                 "Sample rate" : 16000,
@@ -73,7 +73,7 @@
         },
 
         "Voice": {
-            "Passthrough": false,
+            "Passthrough": true,
             "Frame length" : 128,
